."}}, "legacy_curated": true}, {"reference": {"label": "9", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "145", "artid": "377", "page_start": "377", "journal_title": "Z.Phys."}}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "Z.Phys.,A145,377"}], "legacy_curated": true}, {"reference": {"label": "9", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "169", "artid": "492", "page_start": "492", "journal_title": "Z.Phys."}}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "Z.Phys.,A169,492"}], "legacy_curated": true}, {"reference": {"label": "10", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "3", "artid": "109", "page_start": "109", "journal_title": "Found.Phys."}}, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3024414"}, "legacy_curated": true}], "number_of_pages": 14, "referenced_authors_bais": ["R.J.Glauber.1", "H.D.Zeh.1", "Eugene.P.Wigner.1"], "legacy_version": "20190724103801.0", "legacy_creation_date": "2006-06-30", "preprint_date": "1973-04", "author_count": 2, "first_author": {"full_name": "Kuebler, O.", "last_name": "Kuebler", "first_name": "O.", "recid": 2528324}, "control_number": 87063, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0003-4916(73)90040-7"}], "earliest_date": "1973-04", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Kuebler:1973mm"], "abstracts": [{"source": "Elsevier", "value": "The density matrix describing the state of a sybsystem of a physical system whose time dependence is assumed to follow a Schrödinger equation does not itself obey a von Neumann equation. The behavior of the eigenvalues and eigenfunctions of this density matrix is studied. An expression for the rate at which initially separating systems are de-separated is derived in perturbation theory. Indications are given that coherent photon states are more stable in the presence of charged particles than photon number eigenstates. The possible dynamical origin of super selection rules is discussed. A simple model is solved analytically.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "Elsevier"}}], "refereed": true, "external_system